Sure! To compare the declaration flags of your two objects, just pass their stringified forms to the `areDeclarationFlagsIdentical` function. For example:

```ts
const result = areDeclarationFlagsIdentical({
  left: JSON.stringify(parameterObject),
  right: JSON.stringify(variableDeclarationObject)
});
```

If you send me the JSON strings (or the actual objects so I can stringify them), I can run the comparison for you.
